# Fog Harbor Lighthouse — galbook demo story (CC0). 3 choice points, 4 endings, 1 route unlocked after a clear.
title: Fog Harbor Lighthouse
author: galbook demo
license: CC0-1.0

=== prologue Prologue
@bg harbor_night
@bgm calm_sea
After dark the harbor drowns in fog. Only the distant lighthouse still blinks.
You are the courier with the last letter of the day. The envelope reads: "To Shio, keeper of the light."
@show Shio shio_normal center
Shio: "Delivering mail in this fog? ...You've got nerve."
Shio: "The lamp is almost out of oil. I need to fetch some from the warehouse, but the tide has flooded half the path."
? What do you do?
- "I'll come with you." -> help do f.trust += 1; f.brave += 1
- "I'll watch the lamp for you." -> stay do f.trust += 1
- "The letter's delivered. I should go." -> leave
- "...That letter was written to you twenty years ago, wasn't it?" -> secret if s.cleared_light

* help
@hide Shio
@bg path_tide
Cold seawater rises over your ankles. Shio walks ahead, her lantern a blur in the fog.
Shio: "You're so loud when you walk... but thanks."
-> warehouse#

* stay
@bg lamp_room
You stay by the lamp and turn the heavy mirror for her. A ship's horn sounds in the fog, searching for its way.
Shio: "Don't stop the mirror! They can see it!"
$ f.saved_ship = 1
-> warehouse#

* leave
@clear
@bg harbor_night
You leave the letter on the stone step and walk away. When you look back, the light seems dimmer than before.
@end ending A Back in the Fog

=== warehouse Warehouse
@bg warehouse
@show Shio shio_smile center
The warehouse is full of old oil drums, and a stack of unopened letters. All addressed to her.
Shio: "...I never dared open them. In case they say 'stop waiting'."
? Do you encourage her to open them?
- "Open them. Whatever they say, you can bear it." -> open do f.trust += 1
- "If you don't want to, don't. The light is enough." -> keep
- Quietly slip the top letter into her coat pocket -> sneak if f.brave >= 1

* open
Her hands shake as she tears the envelope. Reading, she laughs, then cries.
Shio: "He says... he watches this light every night from across the sea."
-> finale#

* keep
Shio stacks the letters back neatly, like old books.
Shio: "Thank you for not pushing me."
-> finale#

* sneak
She saw you slip the letter into her pocket. She just didn't say anything.
$ f.trust += 2
-> finale#

=== finale Dawn
@bg lamp_room_dawn
The fog lifts. A thin line of gold appears on the horizon.
if f.trust >= 2 -> good
if f.saved_ship == 1 -> ship
-> normal

* good
@cg cg_dawn_together
Shio: "Will you... deliver mail again tomorrow?"
Shio: "I mean, if there's any for me."
$ s.cleared_light = 1
@end ending The Light

* ship
@cg cg_ship
In the harbor sits a ship the light brought home. The captain sends a barrel of fresh oil.
$ s.cleared_light = 1
@end ending Homecoming

* normal
Shio waves at you, then turns to polish the mirror.
@end ending An Ordinary Morning

=== secret Twenty Years Ago
@route Hidden route
@bg lamp_room
@show Shio shio_surprised center
Shio: "...How did you know?"
You turn the envelope over. The postmark's year is the year she came to this lighthouse.
Shio: "So even back then, someone was waiting for my reply."
@cg cg_old_letter
@end ending The Reply
